---
import '../styles/prose.css';

import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Refund policy"
  description="If you buy one of our paid apps, when you can get a refund: accidental purchases, and features that do not work as promised."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Refund policy', path: '/refund-policy/' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-4 sm:pt-10" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,7.5vw,3.75rem)] leading-[1.04] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance"
      >
        Refund policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-label-lg text-on-surface-variant">Last updated October 2026</p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Our promise</h2>
        <p>
          We want every purchase to feel fair. Our rule is simple: a deal should leave neither side
          wronged. You should never pay for something that does not work as we promised. And a refund
          should not be claimed for something that works fine and has been fully used. Everything below
          follows from that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Accidental or unauthorized purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Bought by mistake, or someone else bought without your permission (for example your child)?
          Google Play processes all our payments, so the fastest route is to request the refund directly
          from Google:{' '}
          <a
            href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-link"
          >
            request a refund on Google Play
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Something does not work as promised</h2>
        <p>
          If a feature we advertise does not work for you, talk to us first. Email us your order number
          (it starts with GPA), the purchase date, and what goes wrong. Then give us a fair chance to fix
          it. We will confirm we received your message and tell you what to expect.
        </p>
        <p>
          If we cannot fix it, you can ask for a refund. Requests of this kind must be made within 30 days
          of purchase.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What is not covered</h2>
        <p>
          If the app works as described, the purchase is final once Google's own refund window has passed.
          This policy only covers purchases made through Google Play.
        </p>
        <p>
          Asking for a new feature is not the same as reporting something broken. If you request
          functionality we never advertised, or something that is technically impossible to bring to your
          device or platform, that does not qualify for a refund under this policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          To request a refund or ask anything about this policy, use our{' '}
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or email us at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
          Please include your order number, the purchase date, and a short description of what happened.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
